+//! C2.5 (2026-06-28): pyo3 exposure of the C2 mmap reader.
+//!
+//! The C1a/C2 `MmapSeismicIndex` (`crate::mmap_io::MmapSeismicIndex`) cures the
+//! Path-A anon floor (C2 KEEPS_GATE: anon Δ +0.041 GB ≈ 0, file-resident 96 %,
+//! parity bit-identical, 0.97× latency) — but only behind a Rust bin. The
+//! SEISMIC-150M serving layer (`scripts/seismic_testbed/seismic_federated.py`
+//! → `lib.thinclient.seismic_backend`) cannot call it, so it loads shards via
+//! stock `SeismicIndex.load()` = Path A (owned anon, 912 B/doc → ~137 GB @150M,
+//! unservable on 32 GB). This pyclass closes that gap: it wraps the C2 reader
+//! and exposes a `search` whose return shape *mirrors `PySeismicIndex.search`
+//! exactly* — `Vec<(query_id, score, doc_id)>` — so the federated wrapper /
+//! `SeismicBackend` consume it with zero changes via `--load-mode mmap`.
+//!
+//! Hand-written (not `impl_seismic_index!`-macro): the mmap reader has a
+//! different construction (`from_mmap`, not `build`/`load`) and a different
+//! inner type, so it does not fit the macro. ~80 lines, additive — the owned
+//! path is untouched.
+//!
+//! See `docs/seismic_150m_testbed/07_G3_RAM_FIX_PLAN.md` §4.4 (C2.5) and
+//! `.claude/plans/seismic-c25-pyo3-mmap-binding.md`.
+
